                <pb facs="0748" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6604: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gade</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-24T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 137, March 18, 6 p.m. Department prefers that you should not participate in
                    any conference with your colleagues looking to an arrangement for peace
                    negotiations between Bolsheviki and Latvia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
